tab net | Network | lan

sub tcp | TCP/IP stack

tweak net.tcpglobal | tune | rec
  name  TCP global settings
  desc  Latency-friendly TCP: TCP Fast Open, proportional rate reduction, RACK and tail loss probe, initial window 10, RSS on, timestamps and window-scaling heuristics off. Receive window auto-tuning stays normal.
  C     netsh int tcp set global timestamps=disabled fastopen=enabled fastopenfallback=enabled prr=enabled autotuninglevel=normal rss=enabled
  C     netsh int tcp set global maxsynretransmissions=2 initialRto=2000
  C     netsh int tcp set heuristics wsh=disabled forcews=disabled
  C     netsh int tcp set security mpp=disabled profiles=disabled
  C     netsh int tcp set supplemental internet congestionprovider=default
  C     netsh int tcp set supplemental template=custom icw=10 rack=enabled taillossprobe=enabled
  C     netsh int udp set global uro=disabled uso=enabled
  C     netsh int ipv4 set global taskoffload=enabled defaultcurhoplimit=64 loopbacklargemtu=disabled
  C     netsh int ipv6 set global defaultcurhoplimit=64
  off:
  C     netsh int tcp set global timestamps=default fastopen=default fastopenfallback=default prr=default rss=default maxsynretransmissions=default initialRto=default
  C     netsh int tcp set heuristics wsh=default forcews=default
  C     netsh int tcp set supplemental template=custom icw=default rack=default taillossprobe=default
  C     netsh int udp set global uro=default uso=default
  C     netsh int ipv4 set global loopbacklargemtu=enabled

tweak net.throttle | network_check | rec
  name  Network throttling off
  desc  Stops the multimedia scheduler from capping non-multimedia network traffic while audio or video plays.
  R     NT\Multimedia\SystemProfile | NetworkThrottlingIndex | d:4294967295 | d:10

tweak net.ports | settings_ethernet | rec
  name  More outbound ports
  desc  Raises the highest dynamic port to 65534, so heavy downloads and many connections never run out of ports.
  R     SV\Tcpip\Parameters | MaxUserPort | d:65534 | -

tweak net.afd | send | rec
  name  Winsock send buffers
  desc  Raises the datagram size Winsock sends without copying to 2 KB and keeps dynamic send buffers on, which helps UDP game traffic.
  R     SV\AFD\Parameters | FastSendDatagramThreshold | d:2048 | -
  R     SV\AFD\Parameters | DynamicSendBufferDisable | d:0 | -

tweak net.nagle | bolt | rec
  name  Instant TCP acknowledgements
  desc  Sends TCP ACKs immediately and turns off Nagle batching on wired adapters, lowering latency in online games.
  R     SV\Tcpip\Parameters\Interfaces\* | TcpAckFrequency | d:1 | - | ?wired
  R     SV\Tcpip\Parameters\Interfaces\* | TCPNoDelay | d:1 | - | ?wired

tweak net.tunnels | alt_route | rec
  name  IPv6 tunnel adapters off
  desc  Turns off the Teredo, ISATAP and 6to4 tunnels. Xbox party chat and some peer-to-peer games use Teredo, so leave this off if you play on Xbox Live.
  C     netsh interface teredo set state disabled
  C     netsh interface isatap set state disabled
  C     netsh interface 6to4 set state disabled
  off:
  C     netsh interface teredo set state default
  C     netsh interface isatap set state default
  C     netsh interface 6to4 set state default

tweak net.icmp | alt_route | rec
  name  ICMP redirects off
  desc  Ignores ICMP redirect messages, which a rogue device on your network could use to reroute your traffic.
  R     SV\Tcpip\Parameters | EnableICMPRedirect | d:0 | d:1

tweak net.ipv4 | swap_horiz | reboot
  name  Prefer IPv4
  desc  Makes Windows use IPv4 before IPv6 when a site has both. IPv6 keeps working. Helps with ISPs whose IPv6 routes are slower.
  R     SV\Tcpip6\Parameters | DisabledComponents | d:32 | d:0

tweak net.repair | build | action
  name  Repair network
  desc  Puts the network services back to their normal start types, turns connection checks back on, renews the IP address and flushes the DNS, ARP and NetBIOS caches.
  SVCS  3 | LanmanWorkstation WdiServiceHost NcbService Netman netprofm WwanSvc WinHttpAutoProxySvc vwifibus vwififlt vwifimp
  SVCS  2 | Dhcp DPS lmhosts NlaSvc nsi RmSvc Wcmsvc Winmgmt WlanSvc BFE Dnscache
  R     PW\NetworkConnectivityStatusIndicator | NoActiveProbe | d:0 | -
  R     SV\NlaSvc\Parameters\Internet | EnableActiveProbing | d:1 | -
  R-    M\WcmSvc\wifinetworkmanager\config | AutoConnectAllowedOEM
  R-    PW\WcmSvc\GroupPolicy | fMinimizeConnections
  START Dhcp Dnscache NlaSvc WlanSvc
  DEVON WAN Miniport *|NDIS Virtual Network Adapter Enumerator|Microsoft Wi-Fi Direct Virtual Adapter|Microsoft RRAS Root Enumerator|Microsoft Kernel Debug Network Adapter|Microsoft Radio Device Enumeration Bus
  C     ipconfig /release
  C     ipconfig /renew
  C     arp -d *
  C     nbtstat -R
  C     nbtstat -RR
  C     ipconfig /flushdns
  C     ipconfig /registerdns

tweak net.reset | restart_alt | action risk2
  name  Reset network stack
  desc  Resets Winsock, TCP/IP and the TCP settings to Windows defaults and removes per-adapter Nagle tweaks. Use it when the internet stops working after tweaking. Needs a restart; custom DNS and static IP settings are kept.
  C     netsh winsock reset
  C     netsh int ip reset
  C     netsh int tcp reset
  C     ipconfig /flushdns
  R-    SV\Tcpip\Parameters\Interfaces\* | TcpAckFrequency
  R-    SV\Tcpip\Parameters\Interfaces\* | TCPNoDelay
  R     SV\NetBT\Parameters | EnableLMHOSTS | d:1 | -

sub qos | Traffic priority

tweak net.qos | data_usage | rec
  name  Reserved QoS bandwidth off
  desc  Sets the bandwidth Windows can reserve for QoS traffic to 0%, leaving all of it to your apps.
  R     PW\Psched | NonBestEffortLimit | d:0 | -

tweak net.gameqos | sports_esports | rec
  name  Game traffic priority
  desc  Marks packets from popular online games with DSCP 46 (expedited forwarding), so routers that honour QoS send them first. Covers CS2, Valorant, Fortnite, Apex, CoD, Overwatch 2, Rocket League, League, Dota 2, PUBG, Rust, Siege, Tarkov, GTA V, Roblox, Minecraft, The Finals and Battlefield 2042.
  R     SV\Tcpip\QoS | Do not use NLA | s:1 | -
  QOS   CS2 | cs2.exe
  QOS   Valorant | VALORANT-Win64-Shipping.exe
  QOS   Fortnite | FortniteClient-Win64-Shipping.exe
  QOS   Apex | r5apex.exe
  QOS   ApexDX12 | r5apex_dx12.exe
  QOS   COD | cod.exe
  QOS   Overwatch2 | Overwatch.exe
  QOS   RocketLeague | RocketLeague.exe
  QOS   LoL | League of Legends.exe
  QOS   Dota2 | dota2.exe
  QOS   PUBG | TslGame.exe
  QOS   Rust | RustClient.exe
  QOS   Siege | RainbowSix.exe
  QOS   Tarkov | EscapeFromTarkov.exe
  QOS   GTA5 | GTA5.exe
  QOS   Roblox | RobloxPlayerBeta.exe
  QOS   Minecraft | javaw.exe
  QOS   TheFinals | Discovery.exe
  QOS   Battlefield | BF2042.exe

tweak net.dop2p | share_off | rec
  name  Update sharing (Delivery Optimization) off
  desc  Downloads Windows and Store updates only from Microsoft, without uploading them to or downloading them from other PCs.
  R     PW\DeliveryOptimization | DODownloadMode | d:0 | -

tweak net.dolimits | swap_vert | rec
  name  Delivery Optimization limits
  desc  Caps update downloads at 10% of bandwidth in the background and 70% in the foreground, uploads to other PCs at 50% and 500 GB a month.
  R     CV\DeliveryOptimization\Settings | DOPercentageMaxBackgroundBandwidth | d:10 | -
  R     CV\DeliveryOptimization\Settings | DOPercentageMaxForegroundBandwidth | d:70 | -
  R     CV\DeliveryOptimization\Settings | DOPercentageMaxUploadBandwidth | d:50 | -
  R     CV\DeliveryOptimization\Settings | DOMonthlyUploadDataCap | d:500 | -

tweak net.bits | cloud_sync | rec
  name  BITS bandwidth limit
  desc  Caps background transfers (Windows Update, Store) at 10 KB/s between 8:00 and 17:00 so they never fight your games during the day.
  R     PW\BITS | EnableBITSMaxBandwidth | d:1 | -
  R     PW\BITS | MaxBandwidthValidFrom | d:8 | -
  R     PW\BITS | MaxBandwidthValidTo | d:17 | -
  R     PW\BITS | MaxTransferRateOnSchedule | d:10 | -

sub dns | Name resolution

tweak net.dns | dns | rec
  name  DNS client tuning
  desc  Remembers failed lookups for only 5 seconds, sends queries to all adapters in a fixed order instead of smart reordering, and answers repeated queries without coalescing them.
  R     PM\Windows NT\DNSClient | MaxNegativeCacheTtl | d:5 | -
  R     PM\Windows NT\DNSClient | DisableSmartProtocolReordering | d:1 | -
  R     SV\Dnscache\Parameters | DisableCoalescing | d:1 | -

tweak net.llmnr | travel_explore | rec
  name  LLMNR off
  desc  Turns off Link-Local Multicast Name Resolution. It is rarely needed at home and is a common way to steal password hashes on shared networks.
  R     PM\Windows NT\DNSClient | EnableMulticast | d:0 | -
  R     SV\Dnscache\Parameters | EnableMulticast | d:0 | -

tweak net.netbios | lan | rec
  name  NetBIOS over TCP/IP off
  desc  Turns off the old NetBIOS name service and LMHOSTS lookup on every adapter. Modern file sharing does not need it and it chats on the network constantly.
  R     SV\NetBT\Parameters\Interfaces\* | NetbiosOptions | d:2 | d:0
  R     SV\NetBT\Parameters | EnableLMHOSTS | d:0 | d:1
  R     SV\Dnscache\Parameters | EnableNetbios | d:0 | -

tweak net.wpad | vpn_lock | rec
  name  Proxy auto-discovery off
  desc  Turns off WPAD, which looks for a proxy script on every network. Saves a lookup on connect and closes a known spoofing trick.
  R     CV\Internet Settings\WinHttp | DisableWpad | d:1 | -
  R     UCV\Internet Settings\Wpad | WpadOverride | d:1 | -

tweak net.flushdns | cleaning_services | action
  name  Flush DNS cache
  desc  Clears cached DNS answers. Useful after changing DNS servers or when a site moved.
  C     ipconfig /flushdns

sub nic | Adapter

tweak net.nicpower | energy_savings_leaf | rec desktop
  name  Adapter power saving off
  desc  Turns off Energy Efficient Ethernet, Green Ethernet, selective suspend, wake-on-LAN and the other power features on wired adapters, and stops Windows from powering adapters down.
  R     CC\Class\{4d36e972-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\* | PnPCapabilities | d:24 | - | ?nic
  NICZ  *EEE EEELinkAdvertisement EeePhyEnable AdvancedEEE EnableGreenEthernet *SelectiveSuspend SelectiveSuspend *DeviceSleepOnDisconnect *NicAutoPowerSaver
  NICZ  *ModernStandbyWoLMagicPacket *WakeOnMagicPacket *WakeOnPattern *WakeOnLink *WakeFromPowerOff WakeFromS5 WakeOnLink WakeOnPort WakeOnFastStartup S5ARPOffload S4WakeOnLan S5WakeOnLan EnableWakeOnManagementOnTCO EnablePME
  NICZ  PowerDownPll GigaLite EnableGigaLite ULPMode EnableModernStandby SavePowerNowEnabled EnableSavePowerNow EnableDisconnectedStandby EnableAspm ASPM AutoPowerSaveModeEnabled EnablePowerManagement PowerSaveEnable PowerSaveMode
  NICZ  *EnableDynamicPowerGating DynamicPowerGating EnableD3ColdInS0 EnablePHYFlexibleSpeed EnableD0PHYFlexibleSpeed EnablePHYWakeUp AutoLinkDownPcieMacOff AutoDisableGigabit ReduceSpeedOnPowerDown PowerSavingMode
  NICZ  WakeOnSlot WakeUpModeCap *PMNSOffload *PMARPOffload *PMWiFiRekeyOffload ForceWakeFromMagicPacketOnModernStandby S0MgcPkt AllowAllSpeedsLPLU
  NICS  2 | WolShutdownLinkSpeed
  R     SV\NDIS\Parameters | EnableNicAutoPowerSaverInSleepStudy | d:0 | -
  R     PW\WcmSvc\Local | fDisablePowerManagement | d:1 | -
  R     PW\WcmSvc\GroupPolicy | fDisablePowerManagement | d:1 | -

tweak net.niclatency | speed | rec desktop
  name  Adapter latency settings
  desc  Turns off interrupt moderation, flow control, large send and receive coalescing on wired adapters, keeps checksum offload on and sets sane buffer sizes. Fast 2.5G+ adapters keep interrupt moderation.
  NICZ  *FlowControl *PriorityVLANTag DMACoalescing EnableLLI ApCompatMode *HeaderDataSplit EnableTss EnableCoalesce AdaptiveIFS ITR EnableETW *RscIPv4 *RscIPv6 *LsoV1IPv4 *LsoV2IPv4 *LsoV2IPv6
  NICZ  *InterruptModeration ?slow
  NICZ  OBFFEnabled LatencyToleranceReporting LTROBFF
  NICS  1 | *UdpRsc *UsoIPv4 *UsoIPv6 DropHighlyFragmentedPacket
  NICS  3 | *IPChecksumOffloadIPv4 *TCPChecksumOffloadIPv4 *TCPChecksumOffloadIPv6 *UDPChecksumOffloadIPv4 *UDPChecksumOffloadIPv6
  NICS  1514 | *JumboPacket
  NICS  2048 | *ReceiveBuffers
  NICS  1024 | *TransmitBuffers

tweak net.bindings | hub | rec
  name  Discovery protocols off
  desc  Turns off LLDP and the link-layer topology mapper and responder on all network profiles. Network Map in Control Panel stops working.
  R     SV\Tcpip\Parameters | EnableLLTDIO | d:0 | -
  R     SV\Tcpip\Parameters | EnableRspndr | d:0 | -
  R     PW\LLTD | EnableLLTDIO | d:0 | -
  R     PW\LLTD | EnableRspndr | d:0 | -
  R     PW\LLTD | AllowLLTDIOOnDomain | d:0 | -
  R     PW\LLTD | AllowLLTDIOOnPublicNet | d:0 | -
  R     PW\LLTD | ProhibitLLTDIOOnPrivateNet | d:1 | -
  R     PW\LLTD | AllowRspndrOnDomain | d:0 | -
  R     PW\LLTD | AllowRspndrOnPublicNet | d:0 | -
  R     PW\LLTD | ProhibitRspndrOnPrivateNet | d:1 | -
  BIND  off | ms_lldp ms_lltdio ms_rspndr

tweak net.wifi | wifi_off | rec
  name  Wi-Fi auto-connect off
  desc  Stops Windows from joining open hotspots suggested by Wi-Fi Sense or the PC maker, and drops Wi-Fi when a cable is plugged in.
  R     M\PolicyManager\default\WiFi\AllowAutoConnectToWiFiSenseHotspots | value | d:0 | -
  R     M\WcmSvc\wifinetworkmanager\config | AutoConnectAllowedOEM | d:0 | -
  R     PM\WcmSvc\GroupPolicy | fMinimizeConnections | d:1 | -
  R     M\WcmSvc\wifinetworkmanager\features | WiFiSenseOpen | d:0 | -
  R     M\WcmSvc\wifinetworkmanager\features | PaidWifi | d:0 | -
  R     M\WcmSvc\wifinetworkmanager\features | AllowWiFiHotSpotReporting | d:0 | -

tweak net.newnetwork | wifi_find | rec
  name  New network prompt off
  desc  Stops Windows from asking whether a newly joined network is public or private.
  K+    CC\Network\NewNetworkWindowOff
  off:
  K-    CC\Network\NewNetworkWindowOff

tweak net.bluetooth | bluetooth_disabled | risk2
  name  Bluetooth radio off
  desc  Turns the Bluetooth radio off through policy, for PCs without Bluetooth devices. Also see the Bluetooth services.
  R     M\PolicyManager\default\Connectivity\AllowBluetooth | value | d:0 | d:2
  SVCS  4 | bthserv:3 BthAvctpSvc:3 BTAGService:3 BluetoothUserService:3 BluetoothUserService_* BthA2dp:3 BthEnum:3 BthHFEnum:3 BthLEEnum:3 BTHPORT:3 BTHUSB:3 BthMini:3 BTHMODEM:3 HidBth:3 Microsoft_Bluetooth_AvrcpTransport:3 RFCOMM:3 BthPan:3 bttflt btha4dp ibtsiva

tweak net.wifisvc | wifi_off | risk2
  name  Wi-Fi service off
  desc  Turns off the Wi-Fi service and Wi-Fi Direct, for desktops that only use a cable. Wi-Fi stops working completely.
  SVCS  4 | WlanSvc:2 vwififlt:1 vwifibus vwifimp WFDSConMgrSvc:3 WwanSvc:3

tweak net.vpn | vpn_key_off
  name  VPN & proxy services off
  desc  Turns off the built-in VPN (SSTP, IPsec), remote access and automatic proxy services. Third-party VPN apps such as WireGuard bring their own and keep working.
  SVCS  4 | WinHttpAutoProxySvc:3 RasMan:3 SstpSvc:3 PolicyAgent:3

sub smb | File sharing

tweak net.smb | folder_shared | rec
  name  File sharing tuning
  desc  Removes SMB bandwidth throttling, keeps opportunistic locks on, raises the client command limit and keeps idle connections open for 60 seconds.
  R     SV\LanmanWorkstation\Parameters | DisableBandwidthThrottling | d:1 | -
  R     SV\LanmanWorkstation\Parameters | DisableStrictNameChecking | d:1 | -
  R     SV\LanmanWorkstation\Parameters | KeepConn | d:60 | -
  R     SV\LanmanWorkstation\Parameters | MaxCmds | d:50 | -
  R     SV\LanmanWorkstation\Parameters | EnableOplocks | d:1 | -
  R     SV\LanmanServer\Parameters | Size | d:3 | -
  R     SV\LanmanServer\Parameters | SizReqBuf | d:16384 | -
  R     SV\LanmanServer\Parameters | EnableOplocks | d:1 | -

tweak net.adminshares | folder_off | rec reboot
  name  Admin shares off
  desc  Stops Windows from creating the hidden C$, D$ and ADMIN$ shares at startup. Remote admin tools that rely on them stop working.
  R     SV\LanmanServer\Parameters | AutoShareWks | d:0 | -
